### STATE.md Git Context

STATE.md now tracks git workflow context:

```markdown
## Git Context

- Jira Ticket: PT-1234
- GitHub Issue: #456
- Branch: PT-1234--fix-performance-issue
- Base Branch: ENG-1353--release
- Task Complexity: MODERATE (classified 2026-02-03 10:45)
```

## Model Profiles

Model profiles control which AI model each agent uses:

| Agent                      | quality | balanced | budget |
| -------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------ |
| lu-cognition            | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-router               | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-learner              | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-planner              | opus    | opus     | sonnet |
| lu-roadmapper           | opus    | sonnet   | sonnet |
| lu-executor             | opus    | sonnet   | sonnet |
| lu-phase-researcher     | opus    | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-project-researcher   | opus    | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-research-synthesizer | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-debugger             | opus    | sonnet   | sonnet |
| lu-codebase-mapper      | sonnet  | haiku    | haiku  |
| lu-verifier             | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-plan-checker         | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-integration-checker  | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| dx-advocate                | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| code-simplifier            | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| security-auditor           | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |
| lu-pr-reviewer          | sonnet  | sonnet   | haiku  |

**balanced** (default) - Opus for planning, Sonnet for execution/verification.

> **Current Limitation:** Cursor's Task tool currently only supports `model="fast"` or inheriting from the parent agent. The profiles above are preserved for future compatibility when granular model control becomes available.

**Current model variable values:**

```
# Lightweight agents → use "fast"
learner_model = "fast"
mapper_model = "fast"        # lu-codebase-mapper
synthesizer_model = "fast"   # lu-research-synthesizer

# Reasoning-intensive agents → omit (inherit from parent)
planner_model = (omit)
executor_model = (omit)
verifier_model = (omit)
debugger_model = (omit)
researcher_model = (omit)
roadmapper_model = (omit)
checker_model = (omit)
reviewer_model = (omit)      # dx-advocate, code-simplifier, security-auditor, etc.
```

## Workflow Configuration

Stored in `.planning/config.json`:

```json
{
  "mode": "interactive|yolo",
  "depth": "quick|standard|comprehensive",
  "model_profile": "balanced",
  "cognitive": {
    "enabled": true,
    "memory_recall": true,
    "working_memory": true,
    "intuition_check": true,
    "routing": "auto"
  },
  "workflow": {
    "research": true,
    "plan_check": true,
    "verifier": true,
    "code_review": true,
    "uat_required": true,
    "always_verify": true,
    "capture_learnings": true
  },
  "parallelization": {
    "enabled": true,
    "plan_level": true,
    "task_level": false
  }
}
```

**New cognitive options:**

- `cognitive.enabled` — Enable cognitive pre-flight (default: true)
- `cognitive.memory_recall` — Load from MEMORY.md (default: true)
- `cognitive.working_memory` — Use WORKING.md (default: true)
- `cognitive.routing` — "auto" for complexity-based routing

**New workflow options:**

- `always_verify` — Verification at all complexity levels (default: true)
- `capture_learnings` — Extract to MEMORY.md after verification (default: true)

## Luca Commands (Skills)

### Unified Entry

- `/lu <task | PT-#### | Jira-URL>` — Git setup → Cognitive routing → Execute → PR

**Flags:**

- `--force-complex` — Force full planning pipeline
- `--skip-memory` — Skip memory recall (fresh start)
- `--skip-branch` — Skip branch creation (use current branch)

### Project Lifecycle

- `/lu-new-project` — Full initialization flow + BRAIN.md
- `/lu-new-milestone` — Start next version
- `/lu-complete-milestone` — Archive + consolidate learnings
- `/lu-audit-milestone [V]` — Audit milestone completion against original intent
- `/lu-plan-milestone-gaps` — Create phases to close gaps from audit
- `/lu-map-codebase` — Analyze existing codebase first

### Phase Management

- `/lu-discuss-phase [N]` — Gather context before planning
- `/lu-research-phase [N]` — Deep ecosystem research for niche/complex domains
- `/lu-list-phase-assumptions [N]` — Preview AI planning assumptions before execution
- `/lu-plan-phase [N]` — Create execution plans with cognitive pre-flight
- `/lu-execute-phase [N]` — Execute + always verify + capture learnings
- `/lu-verify-work [N]` — User acceptance testing
- `/lu-add-phase` — Add phase to roadmap
- `/lu-insert-phase [N]` — Insert urgent work
- `/lu-remove-phase [N]` — Remove future phase

### Navigation

- `/lu-progress` — Where am I? What's next?
- `/lu-help` — Command reference

### Session Management

- `/lu-pause-work` — Create context handoff
- `/lu-resume-work` — Resume from handoff
- `/lu-quick` — Execute ad-hoc task

### Utilities

- `/lu-settings` — Configure workflow toggles and model profile
- `/lu-set-profile <profile>` — Quick switch model profile (quality/balanced/budget)
- `/lu-debug` — Memory-aided debugging
- `/lu-add-todo` — Capture idea for later
- `/lu-check-todos` — List pending todos
- `/lu-choose` — Help decide between issue-driven vs Luca workflow
- `/lu-update` — Update Luca to latest version
- `/lu-join-discord` — Join Luca Discord community

### PR Management (NEW)

- `/lu-address-pr [PR]` — Address PR review comments with agent swarm

**Flags:**

- `--dry-run` — Validate and plan only, don't execute or respond
- `--skip-validation` — Skip agent validation, address all comments
- `--category=security` — Only address comments of specific category
- `--no-respond` — Execute fixes but don't post GitHub responses

**Workflow:**

1. Fetch PR comments (inline + general)
2. Categorize by concern type (security, architecture, performance, etc.)
3. Spawn reviewer agents in parallel to validate each concern
4. Aggregate results: valid fixes, disagreements, informational
5. Create fix plan for valid concerns
6. Execute fixes with atomic commits
7. Verify each fix addresses original concern
8. Post responses to all PR comments
9. Push and post summary

**Agent Routing:**

| Category      | Agent                           |
| ------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Security      | security-auditor                |
| Architecture  | architect                       |
| Performance   | performance-engineer            |
| Code Quality  | dx-advocate                     |
| Accessibility | accessibility-expert            |
| Testing       | test-engineer                   |
| General       | lu-pr-reviewer (coordinator) |

## When to Use Luca

**Use `/lu` (unified entry) when:**

- You have a task and want smart routing
- You're not sure which command to use
- You want cognitive pre-flight automatically

**Use specific commands when:**

- You know exactly which phase to plan/execute
- You're doing project initialization
- You need specific workflow control

**Use regular development when:**

- Quick one-off fixes (though `/lu` handles these)
- Simple features that don't need tracking

## Full Workflow Loop

```
Git Context Setup (Step 0)
       │
       ├── Jira ticket → GitHub issue → Branch
       │
       ▼
Cognitive Pre-Flight (Step 1)
       │
       ├── Load BRAIN.md, MEMORY.md
       │
       ▼
Complexity Classification (Step 2)
       │
       ├── TRIVIAL / MODERATE / COMPLEX
       │
       ▼
    Execute (Step 3)
       │
       ▼
    Verify (Step 4 - ALWAYS)
       │
       ├── EXISTS → SUBSTANTIVE → WIRED
       │
       ▼
    Extract Learnings
       │
       ├── Update MEMORY.md
       ├── Clear WORKING.md
       │
       ▼
    Commit & PR (Step 5)
       │
       ├── Commit changes
       └── Offer PR creation
```

